SELECT 106, 'doc_to_slides_outline', 'Document to Slides Outline', '用我：先把文档转成幻灯片大纲（JSON），供 gen_* 渲染。
    别用我：要最终成品直接 doc_to_deck。
Turn a document (.md / .txt / .pdf / .docx) into a validated slides outline.

    Reads the document server-side, then runs two LLM passes (draft → refine)
    producing a 12–15 slide outline JSON. The outline is normalized against the
    selected template''s constraints (page clamp, bullet caps, auto-highlight of
    key numbers). Feed the returned JSON into gen_html_deck / gen_pptx, or use
    doc_to_deck to render both formats in one call.

    Args:
        file_path: Absolute path of the source document.
        template: Template id (business|fashion|tech|health|education|minimal).
        pages: Target slide count (0 = template default, 12–15).

    Returns:
        The normalized outline as a JSON string.', 'python_function', 'custom', '{"function_name": "_run_tool", "code": "from tools.presentation_tools import doc_to_slides_outline\n\n\nasync def _run_tool(**kwargs) -> str:\n    \"\"\"用我：先把文档转成幻灯片大纲（JSON），供 gen_* 渲染。     别用我：要最终成品直接 doc_to_deck。 Turn a document (.md / .txt / .pdf / .docx) into a validated slides outline.      Reads the docume\"\"\"\n    return str(await doc_to_slides_outline.ainvoke({**kwargs}))\n", "args_schema": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": ""}, "template": {"type": "string", "description": "", "default": "business"}, "pages": {"type": "integer", "description": "", "default": 0}}}', '{"type": "object", "properties": {"file_path": {"type": "string", "description": ""}, "template": {"type": "string", "description": "", "default": "business"}, "pages": {"type": "integer", "description": "", "default": 0}}, "required": ["file_path"]}', 'string', NULL, '{"category": "presentation", "order": 21, "section": null, "is_concurrency_safe": true, "output_schema": null, "guard": {"approval": false, "confirmation": false}, "presentation": {}}', TRUE, TRUE, 'builtin-seeder', FALSE, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, '1.0.0', NULL, 'presentation', TRUE, NULL, '["builtin", "presentation"]', '2026-08-25 14:20:15.078097+00:00', '2026-11-11 01:12:26.331924+00:00'
