SELECT 100, 'sql_agent_tool', 'SQL Agent (Chinook)', '用我：用自然语言问 Chinook 业务库（内部先转 SQL，返回结论）。
别用我：要精确 SQL 或查平台库用 pg_query。

Ask a natural-language question and get an answer from a PostgreSQL
database (read-only).

Runs the hand-built LangGraph SQL agent: discovers tables, reads schemas,
generates a PostgreSQL query, double-checks it, executes it read-only, and
explains the result. Handles joins, aggregations, and multi-table questions.
Use for questions like "how many employees are there", "which artist has
the most albums", or "average track length per genre".

Args:
    question: The natural-language SQL question to answer.
    database: Optional PostgreSQL database name to query. Empty uses the
        default (env SQL_POSTGRES_DB, else POSTGRES_DB, else chinook).

Returns:
    The final answer text (not raw query results).

Example:
    >>> sql_agent_tool("Which genre has the longest average track?", database="chinook")', 'python_function', 'custom', '{"function_name": "sql_agent_tool", "code": "# --- imports ---\n\nfrom langchain_core.tools import InjectedToolCallId, StructuredTool, tool\n\ndef sql_agent_tool(question: str, database: str = \"\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    用我：用自然语言问 Chinook 业务库（内部先转 SQL，返回结论）。\n    别用我：要精确 SQL 或查平台库用 pg_query。\n\n    Ask a natural-language question and get an answer from a PostgreSQL\n    database (read-only).\n\n    Runs the hand-built LangGraph SQL agent: discovers tables, reads schemas,\n    generates a PostgreSQL query, double-checks it, executes it read-only, and\n    explains the result. Handles joins, aggregations, and multi-table questions.\n    Use for questions like \"how many employees are there\", \"which artist has\n    the most albums\", or \"average track length per genre\".\n\n    Args:\n        question: The natural-language SQL question to answer.\n        database: Optional PostgreSQL database name to query. Empty uses the\n            default (env SQL_POSTGRES_DB, else POSTGRES_DB, else chinook).\n\n    Returns:\n        The final answer text (not raw query results).\n\n    Example:\n        >>> sql_agent_tool(\"Which genre has the longest average track?\", database=\"chinook\")\n    \"\"\"\n    from langgraph.tool_adapters import run_sql_agent\n    return run_sql_agent(question, database=database or None)", "args_schema": {"question": {"type": "string", "description": ""}, "database": {"type": "string", "description": "", "default": ""}}}', '{"type": "object", "properties": {"question": {"type": "string", "description": ""}, "database": {"type": "string", "description": "", "default": ""}}, "required": ["question"]}', 'string', NULL, '{"category": "database", "order": 74, "section": null, "is_concurrency_safe": true, "output_schema": null, "guard": {"approval": false, "confirmation": false}, "presentation": {}}', TRUE, TRUE, 'builtin-seeder', FALSE, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, '1.0.0', NULL, 'database', TRUE, NULL, '["builtin", "database"]', '2026-08-22 14:30:39.163844+00:00', '2026-11-11 03:05:55.307380+00:00'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM custom_tools WHERE tool_id = 'sql_agent_tool')
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM custom_tools WHERE id = 100);

